# Line endings are pinned by the repository, not left to each machine's
# `core.autocrlf` setting.
#
# Without this, a patch authored on Linux arrives as LF and is silently
# rewritten to CRLF on checkout for Windows contributors. The result applies
# and runs correctly but no longer matches its own checksums, so byte
# verification of a patch fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the
# patch. Pinning it here makes the tree reproducible on every machine and
# retires the "preserve each file's existing line endings" rule, which only
# ever existed because the tree was inconsistent.
#
# `text=auto` still leaves genuinely binary files untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
